## 3.2  Formate/Formic acid
HCOOH/HCOO− is not only a hydrogen storage chemical with high energy density, but is also widely applied in the green synthesis of a range of petrochemicals in modern energy systems [117–119]. Moreover, among all kinds of products from ${\mathrm{CO}}_{2}{\mathrm{RR}}$ , HCOOH possesses the highest profit per mole of electrons, exhibiting good economic prospects in large-scale industrial production [75]. To date, there are many MOF-related catalysts showing remarkable activity and selectivity for the production of HCOOH by $\mathrm{CO}_{2}\mathrm{RR}$ . Several representative examples are shown in Table 3, we will discuss their structure–activity relationships from the perspective of metal composition, such as In, Sn, and Bi.
